Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.25,0:00:18.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I had my girlfriend\Nbake some apple pie.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.87,0:00:19.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Want some?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.10,0:00:31.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roy...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.51,0:00:34.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As you can see,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.39,0:00:36.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this is that which is forbidden.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.06,0:00:39.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I may not know alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.06,0:00:42.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I do know one thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.82,0:00:44.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who commit\Nthat which is forbidden...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.36,0:00:50.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry.\NI haven't done a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.86,0:00:52.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you were planning to try?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.53,0:00:54.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So many died—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.29,0:00:57.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, I killed them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.66,0:00:58.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was war.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.29,0:01:01.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You weren't there.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.83,0:01:02.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.38,0:01:05.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you couldn't stand\Ngoing to war and killing the enemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.92,0:01:08.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you should have chosen\Nduty at the rear, like I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.97,0:01:10.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By becoming a State Alchemist
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.34,0:01:14.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then calling even some of\Nthose people back to this world,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.01,0:01:16.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,did you think it would save you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.81,0:01:18.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good question.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.73,0:01:22.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is performing the forbidden so straightforward
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.81,0:01:24.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that you can just cram for it\Nto be able to pull it off?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.53,0:01:29.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or did you just want to die?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.78,0:01:32.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that's the case, there are easier ways to go about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.87,0:01:39.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As it turns out, I was unable to attempt it,\Nout of fear for my own life.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.83,0:01:41.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course you couldn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.12,0:01:43.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's just the kind of person I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.67,0:01:44.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's true about anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.79,0:01:50.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, there is a better way to use the life I have than this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.80,0:01:54.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maes,\NI've made up my mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.01,0:01:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell me more, Roy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.64,0:02:00.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.56,0:02:02.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, Lt. Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.15,0:02:05.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's okay. I'll wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.28,0:02:11.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Führer!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.28,0:02:15.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You seem to be investigating\Nthe higher levels of the military, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.03,0:02:19.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, in regards to the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.87,0:02:23.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Regarding that matter,\NI took charge of it personally and concluded it's possible that Brig.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.46,0:02:26.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gen. Basque Grand
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.46,0:02:31.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,teamed up with Ishbalan radicals in conducting seditious research.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.13,0:02:33.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you dissatisfied with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.34,0:02:36.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, I, uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.47,0:02:37.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.85,0:02:40.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, is this about\Nthe Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.31,0:02:42.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.43,0:02:46.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It can be surmised that within the military,\Nthere was experimentation with creating Philosopher's Stones
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.19,0:02:49.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that there were various\Nillegal actions taken to that end.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.98,0:02:52.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And it was not all carried out\Nat Brig. Gen. Grand's discretion.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.32,0:02:57.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the very least,\Nthis also falls upon the succession of superior officers over Doctor Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.91,0:03:00.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's possible that these\Npersons were complicit.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.45,0:03:04.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major generals,\Nbrigadier generals, colonels...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.00,0:03:06.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Involved in something like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.83,0:03:07.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.96,0:03:12.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In just the last year, each one has either died or gone missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.55,0:03:16.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, when you consider that\Nthe 5th Laboratory was still operating
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.34,0:03:19.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that just the other day,\NIshbalan refugees were attacked
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.26,0:03:23.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,by someone within the military who employed mercenaries...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.10,0:03:30.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're saying that even now, \Nsome power within the military
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.02,0:03:30.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is attempting to create a Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.07,0:03:34.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If something like that\Never came to light,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.07,0:03:37.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the military would lose its authority!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.41,0:03:41.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm joking! Follow through on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.45,0:03:47.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, someone has been conducting prohibited, top-secret human experimentation
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.79,0:03:50.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then using assassins who call themselves homunculi to wipe out the evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.34,0:03:53.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot overlook such an outrage.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.09,0:03:55.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will purge this corruption.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.05,0:03:57.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.89,0:03:59.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As such, Führer...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.34,0:04:01.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm, Doctor Marcoh, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.81,0:04:04.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'd like to question him for information again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.14,0:04:06.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Juliet...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.39,0:04:09.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will ask that he be brought to Central immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.06,0:04:13.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The truth is, she's the only one who knows where Marcoh is hiding.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.28,0:04:18.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a precaution to prevent me from revealing anything, even if tortured by the enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.41,0:04:21.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well, if you please...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.20,0:04:24.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,uh... Douglas-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.25,0:04:27.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will purge this corruption.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.96,0:04:32.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything\Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.75,0:04:37.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything,\Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.05,0:04:42.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.76,0:04:48.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that\Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.41,0:06:24.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.78,0:06:27.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this means that all the bigwigs who are connected with the 5th Laboratory
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.99,0:06:30.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,either die or turn up missing?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.95,0:06:34.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And there weren't any criminals on the list who had the Uroboros mark on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.04,0:06:37.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sounds like they're talking about some scary stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.96,0:06:41.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to stick my nose into any more trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.22,0:06:47.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, there should still be scientists who worked under Doctor Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.89,0:06:50.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we could find some of them...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.97,0:06:52.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, leave that to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.02,0:06:55.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, about that...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.27,0:06:58.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's like it doesn't\Nreally matter anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.19,0:07:00.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you guys talking about?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.86,0:07:01.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're saying,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.24,0:07:06.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we've had enough of the Philosopher's Stone and homunculi and other dicey stuff like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.32,0:07:10.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And that maybe, it would be smarter to look for a different method.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.41,0:07:12.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That would definitely be smarter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.50,0:07:15.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if you could find it that simply, there wouldn't be any sport in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.12,0:07:19.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There {\i1}is{\i0} one person who might know something about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.09,0:07:20.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.05,0:07:23.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She lives to the south,\Nin a place called Dublith.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.72,0:07:25.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We plan on paying her a visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.63,0:07:28.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elric brothers...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.39,0:07:30.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here, just one stop before Dublith!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.64,0:07:32.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is there something there?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.52,0:07:35.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the holy land of\NAutomail mechanics, Rush Valley!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.52,0:07:37.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've always wanted to go there!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.31,0:07:39.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take me with you! Take me with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.86,0:07:41.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go there by yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.48,0:07:43.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But who's going to pay\Nmy traveling expenses?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.36,0:07:44.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're trying to mooch off of us?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.86,0:07:47.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's okay, isn't it?\NIt's on the way, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.32,0:07:48.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the use?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.99,0:07:50.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yay!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.20,0:07:56.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So those two have finally decided not to get involved in any more dangerous business, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.41,0:07:59.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They must have realized how hard it was for us to guard them.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.71,0:08:00.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh, uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.75,0:08:03.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that were the case,\Nwhat fun would that be?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.88,0:08:08.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is all to keep us from\Nbecoming the next victims.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.05,0:08:12.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pretty sharp for a kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.83,0:08:36.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not going to Dublith?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.75,0:08:39.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we {\i1}are{\i0} going as far as Rush Valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.71,0:08:41.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.17,0:08:42.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.71,0:08:44.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Weren't you going to ask your teacher
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.38,0:08:46.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,about other methods besides the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.51,0:08:48.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we did that, we'd be killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.93,0:08:50.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Killed?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.72,0:08:57.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We never told our teacher about becoming State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.60,0:09:00.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not to mention that if it got out that\Nwe had performed human transmutation...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.61,0:09:04.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'd like to live a little bit longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.90,0:09:07.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would at least like to have fallen in love, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.20,0:09:10.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And even if that weren't the case,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.28,0:09:14.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I get the feeling we shouldn't ask our teacher about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.08,0:09:17.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what are you going to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.62,0:09:22.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a large-scale Ishbalan camp in the mountains to the south.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.50,0:09:25.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm guessing that Scar and\Nthe others are headed there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.21,0:09:27.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going after Scar?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.22,0:09:31.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's said that a Philosopher's Stone was once created at Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.76,0:09:36.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But since they never had alchemy introduced to them in the first place,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.18,0:09:40.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we think it might be possible that they\Ncreated it in a completely different manner.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.89,0:09:44.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to pound on him\Nand make him tell us the secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.94,0:09:49.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, Brother, he really isn't that bad a person.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.07,0:09:51.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's a killer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.07,0:09:53.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And he uses alchemy to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.45,0:09:56.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't let him\Nget away with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.14,0:10:20.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.73,0:10:28.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.48,0:10:32.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you?! You are not of the people of Ishbal, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.86,0:10:34.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, how rude of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.12,0:10:37.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've failed to introduce myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.41,0:10:42.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm the State Alchemist in charge of exterminating this region.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.47,0:10:56.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got a visitor!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.56,0:11:01.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.39,0:11:05.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm so glad you are safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.94,0:11:08.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm impressed that\Nyou survived as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.69,0:11:09.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where have you been up to now?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.07,0:11:14.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are a certain number of us\Nliving in the mountains to the south.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.49,0:11:18.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were planning on\Nvisiting there ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.70,0:11:22.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our countrymen who were in Central were coming to meet us,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.04,0:11:25.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,traveling so as not to catch the military's attention,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.17,0:11:29.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,when along the way,\Nthey heard stories about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.63,0:11:35.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In these last three years,\Nthey say you've been going around killing State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.18,0:11:41.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was State Alchemists who burned down our villages.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.85,0:11:43.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can understand your\Nfeelings of resentment.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.06,0:11:46.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's true!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.61,0:11:53.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These guys are Ishbalans, aren't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.82,0:11:56.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure it's safe to be\Nhanging around in a place like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.28,0:12:01.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Aren't you guys supposed to be living in the designated camps?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.04,0:12:11.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what you are doing is taking out \Nyour anger in sworn vengeance, is it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.09,0:12:15.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Vengeance only sows the seeds of renewed vengeance.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.01,0:12:20.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the ancient words of Ishbala, it says:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.76,0:12:24.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Those who receive pain can still sleep."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.10,0:12:28.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Those who give pain cannot sleep."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.01,0:13:03.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That arm of yours...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.26,0:13:06.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that your brother's arm?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.69,0:13:15.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Why didn't you report to me that the \NElric brothers had been put in a hospital?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.61,0:13:17.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Didn't I mention that?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.86,0:13:19.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, it's no big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.50,0:13:21.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Never mind them,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.50,0:13:21.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No big deal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.24,0:13:24.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it sounds like your posting to Central is going to be formally settled on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.12,0:13:28.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hurry up and make yourself important\Nso you can make things easier for the rest of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.58,0:13:29.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And find yourself a wife!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.42,0:13:31.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be gentle with the telephone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.00,0:13:33.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant, get us a train.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.29,0:13:35.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To Central?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.55,0:13:38.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something is going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.67,0:13:43.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mustang-san is just\Nworried about those two.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.68,0:13:46.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no need to\Nworry him unnecessarily,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.85,0:13:48.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,nor does he need to know\Nabout any of the nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.35,0:13:53.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For one thing, it's possible that our phones are being tapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.69,0:13:57.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, but I still have\Nthings to look into.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.48,0:13:59.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.49,0:14:01.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Papa still has lots of work to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.65,0:14:02.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll be back later.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.49,0:14:08.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bring me the materials\Non the Liore riots!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.04,0:14:09.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.95,0:14:13.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where are the diagrams of the \Ntransmutation circles from the 5th Laboratory?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.42,0:14:16.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The budget from the first year of the Ishbal Rebellion!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.59,0:14:21.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Am I going to get\Novertime pay for this?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.26,0:14:22.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll give you a picture of Elicia!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.22,0:14:32.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ishbal... Liore... Mugear's mines...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.06,0:14:36.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once they got near a Philosopher's Stone,\Nthey were destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.98,0:14:38.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Strange, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.61,0:14:42.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they're driving people to\Ncreate a Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.78,0:14:46.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,why would they spread stories around\Nthat destruction befalls those who seek the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.33,0:14:49.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it to get rid of all the evidence?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.50,0:14:52.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No... It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.08,0:14:54.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,just the opposite, could it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.29,0:14:57.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Supposing everything was reversed...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.67,0:15:03.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on... The unit that caused \Nthe outbreak of war in Ishbal was...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.72,0:15:05.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...Douglas? Where have\NI heard that name before?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.01,0:15:08.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, there's a phone call\Nfrom the Führer's secretary.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.39,0:15:13.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, Doctor Marcoh has arrived in Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.94,0:15:15.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He is waiting at the hotel.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.52,0:15:18.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.\NI will go see him right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.24,0:15:24.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Douglas... Juliet...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.28,0:15:27.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.24,0:15:30.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Put all of these materials back where you found them!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.12,0:15:32.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once that's done, you can go home!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.75,0:15:34.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Also, you're fired!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.25,0:15:35.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't ever come around here again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.75,0:15:41.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry to put you\Nthrough all this trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.50,0:15:43.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ms. Secretary... Douglas-san,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.30,0:15:46.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,do you know much\Nabout the Ishbalan War?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.84,0:15:49.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I have always had desk jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.80,0:15:50.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So have I, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.89,0:15:54.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've been looking into\Nsome things lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.68,0:15:59.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you know that the reason the rebellion broke out
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.94,0:16:02.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was that one of the soldiers stationed there recklessly shot and killed an Ishbalan child?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.44,0:16:07.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That soldier's name, \Nit turns out, was Juliet Douglas.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.49,0:16:10.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a common name.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.78,0:16:12.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's where it gets interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.62,0:16:14.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The soldier with that name
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.37,0:16:17.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was supposed to have died two years before the Ishbal Rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.37,0:16:19.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is odd.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.92,0:16:21.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's one other "odd" thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.42,0:16:24.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Douglas was dead before then.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.01,0:16:28.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet the muster roll for this person\Nnamed Juliet Douglas was never withdrawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.51,0:16:32.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the contrary,\Nover the last two years,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.68,0:16:35.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the soldier with that name\Nhas been suddenly promoted.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.60,0:16:40.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And now, she has been promoted to the Führer's Ministerial Secretary?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.77,0:16:43.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.61,0:16:46.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Were you at Ishbal?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.61,0:16:50.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or did you just use Douglas's \Nregistration to get into the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.70,0:16:53.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Doctor is waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.08,0:16:58.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that even Marcoh\Nbehind that door?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.21,0:17:02.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.00,0:17:05.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or perhaps, "farewell"\Nmight be more appropriate.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.71,0:17:08.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a cool tattoo\Nyou've got there, sweetheart.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.34,0:17:13.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.65,0:17:22.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was unexpectedly skillful, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.44,0:17:26.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sloth, make sure to let everyone know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.95,0:17:33.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Ross,\Nthey're right next to the Führer!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.53,0:17:36.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The enemy has fully infiltrated the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.24,0:17:39.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their purpose...\Nis not to create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.17,0:17:42.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.83,0:17:43.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.13,0:17:44.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.13,0:17:48.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, dammit...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.17,0:17:51.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez, what a pain...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.05,0:17:55.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? He's not there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.06,0:17:58.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He left for Central with Lieutenant Hawkeye.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.56,0:17:59.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Has something happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.85,0:18:02.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With this information,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.73,0:18:05.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he had a chance to rise\Nright to the top!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.23,0:18:07.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any event, we should get to someplace safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.73,0:18:08.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.86,0:18:11.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though\NI've got nothing left to hang onto.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.11,0:18:14.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't you\Ntell me all about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.20,0:18:18.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Lieutenant has a mole under one of her eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.25,0:18:21.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.25,0:18:23.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I must have gotten careless.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.13,0:18:31.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.31,0:18:42.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.06,0:18:45.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have a wife and daughter waiting for me at home.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.11,0:18:54.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a pretty good act,\Nwasn't it, Lt. Colonel Hughes?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.88,0:19:11.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to become the Führer.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.34,0:19:15.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to change\Nthe way this country runs.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.55,0:19:17.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the only thing I can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.51,0:19:23.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you'll need someone who\Nunderstands you and can support you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.85,0:19:29.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone underneath you, who can push you upward.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.41,0:20:22.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama, why?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.49,0:20:24.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are they burying Papa?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.91,0:20:29.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Why are those men burying Papa?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.75,0:20:30.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.00,0:20:32.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elicia...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.00,0:20:35.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want them to.\NI don't want them to!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.13,0:20:39.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they do that, then Papa\Ncan't do his work anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.89,0:20:41.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama, stop them!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.01,0:20:43.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elicia...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.47,0:20:46.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Papa said he still had\Na lot of work to do!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.89,0:20:48.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want them to!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.31,0:20:51.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't bury him! Mama!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.94,0:20:52.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Papa!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.48,0:20:54.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Papa!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.25,0:21:15.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Killed in the line of duty and\Nposthumously promoted two ranks...\NBrigadier General Hughes, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.92,0:21:20.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What am I going to do\Nnow that the man who said
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.76,0:21:24.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he would stay beneath me and assist me\Nhas gone above me, you idiot?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.85,0:21:26.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.52,0:21:32.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once, I tried putting together a theory\Non how to perform human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.86,0:21:36.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just now, I was frantically remembering it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.78,0:21:39.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We alchemists are nasty creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.61,0:21:43.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If the Elric brothers\Nwere mixed up in this,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.12,0:21:45.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,why didn't he report it to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.83,0:21:48.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He didn't have to go\Ncharging into this alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.25,0:21:52.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Haven't you figured it out yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.63,0:21:54.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Figured what out?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.34,0:21:57.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When it comes to those brothers,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.17,0:22:01.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel has been known to\Nlose his level-headed judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.34,0:22:05.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, Brigadier General Hughes
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.72,0:22:09.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,took everything concerning\Nthe Elric brothers upon himself,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.81,0:22:13.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so that the Colonel could relax\Nand set his sights above himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.16,0:22:24.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's starting to rain, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.41,0:22:29.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.46,0:22:42.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if this is like the food that Mom used to make.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.13,0:22:47.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hughes-san, his wife, and Elicia-chan were all such fine people.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.76,0:22:48.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.76,0:22:50.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.18,0:22:52.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Hughes is a mother hen and a busybody. He bothers me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.98,0:22:55.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He always used to come to joke around with us, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.60,0:22:58.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Every day, he said\Nhe was busy with work,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.36,0:23:00.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but he still always\Ncame by to check on us.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.57,0:23:04.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder why he looked after us\Nas much as he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.57,0:23:05.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who knows?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.07,0:23:08.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When we get back to Central, make sure you thank him.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.68,0:23:26.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.18,0:23:29.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is something the matter, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.22,0:23:32.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nope.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.13,0:25:29.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.43,0:25:33.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 26: "Her Reason"
Dialogue: 0,0:25:33.51,0:25:36.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never even thought about it.\NCould there be somebody\Nwho felt that way about me?
